      "writtenOn": "2018-10-07T01:10:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only command we can ever send on this special address is \"send ITE programming sequence\"?\n\nSeems like we should at least look at the first byte of written data as a command code.  0x00 \u003d send ITE programming sequence, 0x01-0xFF\u003dreserved.\n\nOtherwise, when it turns out that the next ITE chip requires a slightly different sequence, how will we handle that?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "6be66400760d0203d8dcfc6773f6d6e83e0c7c59",
